body:
@Niko1221 I kept this submission focused on one optional near-tail checkpoint at an existing prefill boundary. The paired code/doc/chat gate is bitwise identical on the recorded fixed-placement setup; the three timing pairs show 17.047 → 4.470 s branch TTFT on the 33.8k fixture, with a +0.93% fresh-prompt cost. The PR links the complete evidence and its limits.

Before submitting, I also checked the related work: root retention (#62/#65), async checkpoint copying (#203), and VMM/cache work (#37, #378, #563). I found no equivalent near-tail checkpoint in the public branches inspected.

We also have a separately validated automatic elastic expert-cache port (stable VMM addresses, fixed core/rotating tail, growth/shrink at safe points), but I have not opened another cache PR because that overlaps your planned work in #533 and the existing VMM proposals. Your stated preference there is manual VRAM control. If the automatic variant's measurements or a focused part of its implementation would be useful, the same linked report includes the patch, provenance, CUDA functional checks and isolated numeric comparison. We can shape a follow-up around the direction you prefer.
